Lesson 1: Basic Directory Navigation (Linux)
pwd

Shows your current working directory

pwd


Example output:

/home/username

mkdir

Create a directory

mkdir -v dir1


-v → verbose (shows what is created)

Create multiple directories with parents:

mkdir -vp dir2/dir3/dir4


-p → creates parent directories if needed

ls

List directory contents

ls


Recursive listing:

ls -R


-R → shows subdirectories too

cd

Change directory

cd dir2
cd dir3


Useful shortcuts:

cd ..   # move to parent directory
cd -    # move to previous directory
cd      # move to home directory

Summary

pwd → where you are

mkdir → create directories

ls → list files/directories

cd → move between directories
